A discovery method can narrow the plausible economic relationships without
settling the effect of a proposed action. The comparisons here examine what
changes when the variables are continuous, relationships are nonlinear, or
important customer circumstances are unobserved. The practical choice depends
on those assumptions as well as the computation.

